; Backus-Naur Form Grammar for the Build Variants extension
; https://semver.xyz/extensions/variants/
;
; A Build Variant is ordinary <build> metadata (see VERSION.bnf) whose
; identifiers name deployment-target axes, ordered coarse-to-fine so that the
; core Build Channels rule (a "+ <build>" on a comparator/tilde/caret) selects
; a coherent subset by prefix:
;   ^1.0.0+linux        ->  every linux variant in the 1.x line
;   ^1.0.0+linux.x64    ->  narrows to linux/x64 (any abi)
;   1.2.0+win32.x64     ->  one exact artifact
; The fixed axes MUST appear in order (os, then arch, then abi); any fixed axis
; may be omitted only if every later fixed axis is also omitted, so a variant is
; always a PREFIX of the axis sequence. An omitted axis is no constraint.
; "wasm32" stands alone as the whole platform: a WebAssembly build is not tied
; to an operating system.
;
; Qualifiers follow the fixed axes. A floor ("glibc.2.28", "musl.1.2",
; "osv.11.0", "napi.8") means "this value or later"; an exact tag ("node.127",
; "electron.123") must match the target exactly; any other identifier is a
; feature tag ("avx2", "cuda"). Floors are plain numeric identifiers, so they
; compare numerically under the core precedence rules.
;
; Target matching (which variant suits a machine) is defined in the extension:
; a variant applies when every coordinate it states is satisfied by the target,
; and the most specific applicable variant of the highest applicable release
; wins.

<variant build> ::= <platform> ( "." <qualifier> )*

<platform>      ::= <os> ( "." <arch> ( "." <abi> )? )?
                  | "wasm32"

<os>            ::= "linux" | "darwin" | "win32" | "freebsd" | "openbsd"
                  | "android" | "sunos" | "aix"

<arch>          ::= "x64" | "arm64" | "arm" | "ia32" | "ppc64" | "s390x"
                  | "riscv64" | "loong64"

; "arm" is ARMv7, what process.arch reports for ARMv6 and ARMv7 alike.

<abi>           ::= "glibc" <floor version>?
                  | "musl" <floor version>?
                  | "msvc"

<qualifier>     ::= <floor> | <exact tag> | <feature>

<floor>         ::= ( "osv" | "napi" ) <floor version>

<floor version> ::= "." <numeric identifier> ( "." <numeric identifier> )?

<exact tag>     ::= ( "node" | "electron" ) "." <numeric identifier>

; A feature tag is any build identifier (see VERSION.bnf). Lowercase is
; conventional; tags SHOULD be sorted for a canonical form.
<feature>       ::= <build identifier>
